.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH "bead list" 1  "bead list " 
.SH NAME
bead list \- List issues
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbead list\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-\-status\fR] [\fB\-\-assignee\fR] [\fB\-\-ready\fR] [\fB\-\-sort\fR] [\fB\-\-blocked\fR] [\fB\-\-comments\fR] [\fB\-\-fields\fR] [\fB\-\-notes\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-search\fR] [\fB\-\-count\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List issues with optional filtering and comment projection.
.PP
Supports filtering by status, assignee, ready frontier, and manual block. Uses claim
ordering (priority ASC, created_at ASC, id ASC) for deterministic results by
default. Ready frontier uses the same ordering as \*(Aqbead claim\*(Aq but is read\-only
and does not reserve work. With \*(Aq\-\-ready \-\-sort attempts\*(Aq, consecutive failures
order beads within each priority tier before the FIFO tie\-breakers.
.PP
EXAMPLES:
  bead list \-\-json \-\-limit 10                      # First 10 issues as one JSON array
  bead list \-\-jsonl \-\-limit 10                     # First 10 issues as JSON objects per line
  bead list \-\-status open \-\-assignee alice        # Open issues assigned to alice
  bead list \-\-ready \-\-limit 5                      # Next 5 ready candidates
  bead list \-\-ready \-\-sort attempts \-\-limit 5      # Prefer fresh work within priority
  bead list \-\-blocked                               # Manually blocked open issues
  bead list \-\-comments unresolved \-\-json \-\-limit 20  # Issues with unresolved comments
  bead list \-\-all \-\-search TEXT                    # Full\-text search (= \*(Aqbead search TEXT\*(Aq)
  bead list \-\-ready \-\-count                        # How many issues are ready
  bead ready                                        # Shortcut for \*(Aqbead list \-\-ready\*(Aq
  bead search TEXT                                  # Shortcut for \*(Aqbead list \-\-all \-\-search TEXT\*(Aq
.PP
FILTERS:
  \-\-status VALUE    Filter by base status: open, in_progress, deferred, closed
                    (Special case: \*(Aqblocked\*(Aq is an alias for \-\-blocked)
  \-\-assignee NAME   Filter by assignee (exact match)
  \-\-ready           Show only ready frontier issues (open, unassigned, not blocked)
  \-\-sort attempts   Within each priority, show fewer consecutive failures first
  \-\-blocked         Show only manually blocked open issues
  \-\-limit N         Maximum results (0\-999999, default: 100)
  \-\-all             Ignore \-\-limit and return every matching issue
  \-\-search TEXT     Case\-insensitive match against title, description, notes
  \-\-count           Print only the number of matching issues
.PP
COMMENT PROJECTION:
  \-\-comments none         Show only counts and resolution metadata (default)
  \-\-comments unresolved   Include bodies for unresolved comments only
  \-\-comments all          Include all comment bodies in canonical order
.PP
FIELD PROJECTION:
  \-\-fields a,b,c          Emit only the named cli_issue document members (per
                          record for list) in text, \-\-json, and \-\-jsonl
                          output. Unknown names exit 2 naming the valid set;
                          the set is published by the field guide:
                            bead schema explain urn:bead\-rs:schema:issue:native\-v1
                          Without \-\-fields every member is emitted.
.PP
NOTES PROJECTION:
  Appended history belongs in comments (R010), not notes: JSON consumers
  re\-read notes in full, so keep notes bounded context.
  \-\-notes auto            Default. \-\-json/\-\-jsonl keep the full notes member
                          (unchanged NEEDLE contract); text views print the
                          last 2000 characters preceded by an omission line
  \-\-notes none            Omit the notes member entirely
  \-\-notes tail:N          Last N characters of notes
  \-\-notes all             The full notes member
.PP
OUTPUT:
  Without \-\-json: human\-readable table format
  With \-\-json: one compact JSON array, including when empty
  With \-\-jsonl: one compact JSON object per line; empty results write no bytes
  \-\-json and \-\-jsonl cannot be combined
  JSON output includes: id, title, priority, status, manual_blocked, effective_status,
  assignee, dependencies, created_at, updated_at, and labels based on comment projection.
  \-\-count overrides every other output mode: plain text prints an integer,
  \-\-json/\-\-jsonl print one object: {"count": N}.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output one JSON array
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Output one JSON object per line (empty results write no bytes)
.TP
\fB\-\-status\fR \fI<STATUS>\fR
Filter by status
.TP
\fB\-\-assignee\fR \fI<ASSIGNEE>\fR
Filter by assignee
.TP
\fB\-\-ready\fR
Show only ready frontier issues
.TP
\fB\-\-sort\fR \fI<ORDER>\fR
Ready\-frontier ordering: attempts prefers fewer consecutive failures within each priority tier, then retains the FIFO tie\-breakers
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
attempts
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-blocked\fR
Show only manually blocked open issues
.TP
\fB\-\-comments\fR \fI<COMMENTS>\fR [default: none]
Comment projection: none, unresolved, or all (default: none)
.TP
\fB\-\-fields\fR \fI<FIELDS>\fR
Comma\-separated projection of cli_issue document members (FIELD PROJECTION); without it every member is emitted
.TP
\fB\-\-notes\fR \fI<MODE>\fR [default: auto]
Notes projection: auto, none, tail:N, or all (default: auto)
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR [default: 100]
Maximum number of issues to return (0\-999999)
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Ignore \-\-limit and return every matching issue
.TP
\fB\-\-search\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR
Case\-insensitive text search across title, description, and notes
.TP
\fB\-\-count\fR
Print only the number of matching issues (ignores \-\-limit/\-\-all)
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show diagnostic information about filtering (SQL query, counts, exclusion reasons)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
